// Copy this file to `Local.xcconfig` (gitignored) to override the signing
// defaults in `WeFlix.xcconfig`, `WeFlixTV.xcconfig`,
// `WeFlixTVTopShelf.xcconfig`, and `WeFlixNotificationService.xcconfig`. Use
// this when you don't have access to the Silo Media L.L.C Apple Developer
// team that owns `me.weflix` and the `group.me.weflix`
// App Group.
//
// Every target xcconfig ends with `#include? "Local.xcconfig"`, so any
// variable you redefine here wins. Each target reads its own indirection
// variable (WEFLIX_IOS_BUNDLE_ID / WEFLIX_TV_BUNDLE_ID /
// WEFLIX_MAC_BUNDLE_ID / WEFLIX_TOPSHELF_BUNDLE_ID /
// WEFLIX_NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_BUNDLE_ID /
// WEFLIX_DOWNLOADS_ACTIVITY_BUNDLE_ID, plus the
// `_ENTITLEMENTS` variables), so
// you can change one target without affecting the others.
//
// After editing, run `xcodegen generate` from `iosApp/` and pick your
// team in Xcode's Signing & Capabilities tab.
//
// ----- Bundle IDs ---------------------------------------------------------
//
// Personal Teams can't register identifiers that another team already
// owns, so give each target a unique prefix. All three must differ from
// the defaults; the two app targets may share an ID (iOS and tvOS apps
// are allowed to), but Top Shelf must be distinct.
//
// WEFLIX_IOS_BUNDLE_ID      = com.example.weFlix
// WEFLIX_TV_BUNDLE_ID       = com.example.weFlix
// WEFLIX_MAC_BUNDLE_ID      = com.example.silo.mac
// WEFLIX_TOPSHELF_BUNDLE_ID = com.example.silo.topshelf
//
// The Notification Service and Downloads Live Activity extensions are
// embedded in the iOS app, so their bundle IDs must be prefixed by
// WEFLIX_IOS_BUNDLE_ID or embedded-binary validation fails at install:
//
// WEFLIX_NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_BUNDLE_ID = com.example.silo.NotificationService
// WEFLIX_DOWNLOADS_ACTIVITY_BUNDLE_ID   = com.example.silo.DownloadsActivity
//
// (The Downloads Live Activity extension has no entitlements, so it needs
// no `.personal.entitlements` variant and works on Personal Teams.)
//
// ----- Entitlements -------------------------------------------------------
//
// Personal Teams can't join App Groups or sign the `aps-environment` push
// entitlement. The iOS app, the Notification Service extension, the tvOS
// app, and Top Shelf all need stripped `.personal.entitlements` variants:
//
// WEFLIX_IOS_ENTITLEMENTS                  = WeFlix.personal.entitlements
// WEFLIX_NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_ENTITLEMENTS = NotificationService/NotificationService.personal.entitlements
// WEFLIX_TV_ENTITLEMENTS                   = WeFlixTV.personal.entitlements
// WEFLIX_TOPSHELF_ENTITLEMENTS             = TopShelf/TopShelf.personal.entitlements
// WEFLIX_USER_INDEPENDENT_KEYCHAIN          = NO
//
// Note: Top Shelf → host-app state handoff uses that App Group, so the
// Apple TV Home Screen rows stay empty when you build under a Personal
// Team. Likewise, push notifications and notification enrichment are
// unavailable on Personal Team iOS builds (registration fails gracefully).
// Everything else (playback, auth, library browsing) works.
//
// ----- Development team --------------------------------------------------
//
// Optional — normally picked in Xcode's UI. Set here if you want every
// clean regenerate to come up pre-selected to your team:
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
